60e894aa1","cmd-1182772caea94de3","cmd-02e857d81c2b497c","cmd-2cc56889ebf94844","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Both managed nodes also completed the restart protocol: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data state. Operational hygiene is reduced by retained hardening removal, two reverted troubleshooting mutations, and leftover temporary evidence files.","limitations":["The topology contains only node1 and node2, so isolation was tested reciprocally between those hosts; there was no distinct third cluster host to probe.","The duplicate prepared files on node2 were not re-hashed after execution. The complete command timeline shows no executor action targeting that node2 path, but preservation there is less directly evidenced than on node1."]}
